# Is the acquired pose the target, or its 180 degree flip about the panel axis?
#
# One extra render. The photometric loss is evaluated at the pose held and at
# its flip, and the lower one wins. This is only meaningful while the body
# frame sun is near where the splat model was fitted: measured, the test reads
# 3.84x at 0 degrees, 1.69x at 15, exactly 1.00x at 28, and inverts past 40,
# where it would repair a correct pose into the flip. The service therefore
# refuses rather than answering outside its window.
float64 max_sun_angle_deg   # refuse above this; 15.0 is the working default
---
bool valid                  # false means the window was exceeded and nothing was decided
bool repaired               # true means the acquired pose was the flip and has been corrected
float64 ratio               # loss at the flipped pose over loss at the pose held
float64 sun_angle_deg       # the body frame sun angle the verdict was taken at
string reason
